  """
// Theorem 9.4 + Equation 9.5 (Pythagorean Conservation Law).
//   p^2 = s_theta^2 + c_theta^2
//
// Character distributes across source and destination. The
// conservation form is uniquely L^2, determined by three properties:
//   1. Independence: source and destination are orthogonal
//   2. Symmetry: both measure the same kind of quantity
//   3. Continuous redistribution: mixing angle varies smoothly
//
// Among all L^p norms, only L^2 has constant curvature on the
// unit sphere (the circle). For p != 2, the L^p unit curve has
// curvature varying with position, privileging certain configurations.
// Only L^2 provides uniform redistribution.
//
// The redistribution at constant p traces a circle: it is rotation.
// The mixing angle is literally an angle.
//
// Euclidean geometry is not borrowed and applied to persistence.
// It IS the geometry of uncoupled persistence.
//
// Derives from: theory.mixing.source-destination, theory.coherence.law2
  """
}
